<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Auto Backup rules for Android 11 and below (`android:fullBackupContent`).
  Android 12+ uses `data_extraction_rules.xml` instead — both are needed, and
  both must exclude the same thing.

  Offline map packs live in `getExternalFilesDir(null)/maps/` and run from 3 MB
  to 356 MB each. Auto Backup's quota is 25 MB per app, and exceeding it makes
  the system skip the backup *entirely* — silently. One median-sized pack would
  therefore stop the expenses/rides/vehicles database from ever being backed up,
  with nothing to tell the rider.

  Packs are re-downloadable from index.json, so there is nothing of value to
  back up here anyway. See spec/drawing_from_local_tiles.md, "Хранение паков".

  `dash_config.xml` is the dash WiFi settings (DashConfig), excluded for two
  reasons that happen to be the same exclusion:

  - the passphrase. The factory one is `12345678` and no secret, but overriding
    it is a supported feature, and since task 7.3 these are stored in the clear
    — the encrypted store they used to live in was protecting nothing while
    silently reverting a rider's saved dash whenever the Keystore refused;
  - restoring it would break the migration that reads what that store left
    behind. The blobs travel inside this file; their Keystore master key does
    not. On a new phone they would be permanently undecryptable, so the
    migration would retry on every attach and warn into every ride file forever
    about settings that had long since been re-entered.

  Cost of excluding it, stated fully: a new phone asks the rider to pick the
  dash from the system dialog once — that is the out-of-the-box path anyway —
  AND an overridden passphrase or prefix does not come along, so a rider who
  changed either has to enter it again. That is the same trade as the first
  bullet, seen from the other side: a secret that never leaves the device also
  never arrives on the next one. The failure mode if they forget is a bare WiFi
  auth error, so it is worth knowing about.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="external" path="maps/" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="dash_config.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
